# Customer close account (learned 2026-09-29)

**Invariant:** Customer “Cancel Membership” / close login = **delete Supabase Auth user** + clear VIP override / likes / carts. **Never delete `orders`.** Admin Users drops the row because VIP roster is Auth-synced. Past purchases remain in Admin → Orders (email / order id).

## Two delete paths (do not mix)

| Path | Auth | Orders | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `POST /api/me/close-account` | Deleted | **Kept** | Customer self-service |
| `DELETE /api/admin/supabase-users` + `deletePublicDataForAuthUser` | Deleted | **Deleted** | Admin hard delete (tests / ops) |

## Where orders live after close

- Supabase `orders` table (unchanged)
- Admin → Orders (search by email / order id)
- Not on Admin → Users (no Auth → not in `authVipEmailSet`)

## UI copy

Say login is closed and order records may remain for legal/business reasons — do not claim “all related data deleted.”

## Cousins

- Local-only demo profiles without Auth UUID: local `deleteUser` only
- VIP `vip_manual_grade_overrides` cleared by email on close
- Admin hard-delete still cascades orders — intentional ops tool, not customer UX
